# Portfolio blueprint operating directives

Before generating or changing UI, layout, styling, or page structure in this repo:

1. Read [PROJECT_BLUEPRINT.md](../../PROJECT_BLUEPRINT.md) and follow its tokens, typography, section architecture, and CAD/HUD patterns (including `<Plus />` corner crosshairs and semi-transparent 1px blueprint borders on structural cards).
2. Use https://www.sutera.ch/ as the structural reference for numbered domains, metadata strips, and HUD-style interactivity—do not invent spacing or colors outside the blueprint.

When you change theme tokens, tech stack, or page architecture:

3. Update [PROJECT_BLUEPRINT.md](../../PROJECT_BLUEPRINT.md) in the same change set.
4. Append a dated entry to the Change Log in [MEMORY.md](../../MEMORY.md) describing what changed and why.

Stack default unless the blueprint is updated first: React (Vite), Tailwind CSS, Framer Motion, `lucide-react`.
